WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:11.948
Fourier showed that every periodic signal is a sum of sines. With one, three and ten terms, the sum gets closer and closer to a square.

2
00:00:12.346 --> 00:00:22.425
The FFT computes the spectrum of a block of N samples. Its points, the bins, are spaced by the sampling rate divided by N: that is the resolution.

3
00:00:23.129 --> 00:00:34.128
Two sines 30 hertz apart merge into a single peak with N of 1024, and separate with N of 8192. More resolution requires longer blocks.

4
00:00:34.829 --> 00:00:45.750
The window smooths the edges of the block. Without a window, the energy of a sine that falls between two bins leaks all over the spectrum; Hann and Blackman reduce that leakage at the cost of slightly wider peaks.
